  "authoringNote": "Partial S3 snapshot (D5 valid correction). f13x1-order v1 is a valid final order whose item code K0822 is used only as a mismatching synthetic value (recorded ruling 8); no code recommendation or coverage claim is made. v2 supersedes v1 under C08 (same ID and kind, both metadata subjects the case, earlier target) and states K0823 with a corrected description; the receipt links v2. Superseded list [f13x1-order v1]; quarantine empty. R01 evaluates only current versions (pack /rules/0/applicability/condition, C09), so the old code is not current evidence: R01 passes with no R01.order_item_code_disagrees, citing the seven supplier fields and v2 /item/code (8). R02 to R05 pass on v2, the encounter and the receipt with the standard citation sets (6, 9, 6, 4). R09 passes: every version is available, application/json, hash-matching and parseable. R06 is manual_review for the qualified_clinical_reviewer with R06.clinical_review (no refs, effect none) and cites the five /clinical/ statements of the usable encounter; R07 passes citing /lcmpReport/incorporated (false; the null evaluationDate is not cited); R08 passes; R10 is not_applicable with R10.pure_assessment. clinicalReviewRequired is true. Every parent is empty. v1 contributes no fact or citation. State ready_for_review. Recorded reading: a rule cites evidence-field facts only from the documents it reads, and R04 reads only final current usable records; every usable encounter and order here is final, so no draft is excluded. The standard chronology holds: the order date 2026-09-08 is after the 2026-08-24 encounter (not the same day, so C02 does not apply) and inside the C01 bound 2027-02-24, and the receipt at 2026-09-09T16:30:00Z is after the C06 span of the order date, which ends 2026-09-09T12:00Z. Deferred to S4: arrival-order recovery, history display, replay and rollback prevention are not exercised; human acceptance is a separate workflow action.",
